WEBVTT

00:00.459 --> 00:01.667
- [Voiceover] What I
wanna do in this video

00:01.667 --> 00:05.126
is figure out multiple
ways to express the area

00:05.126 --> 00:07.402
of the entire large rectangle,

00:07.402 --> 00:11.535
which we see is made up of
these six smaller rectangles.

00:11.535 --> 00:13.369
So there's a couple of
ways that we can do it.

00:13.369 --> 00:15.104
One way is, we can just
multiply the height

00:15.104 --> 00:18.942
of this big rectangle times the
width of this big rectangle.

00:18.942 --> 00:20.242
So what's its height?

00:20.242 --> 00:22.842
Well, from here to here,

00:22.842 --> 00:25.420
that distance is going to be y squared,

00:25.420 --> 00:27.091
and then from there to there,

00:27.091 --> 00:30.481
that distance is going to be negative 6y.

00:30.481 --> 00:31.387
And I know what you're thinking.

00:31.387 --> 00:34.080
How can my distance be negative 6y?

00:34.080 --> 00:36.379
Isn't a distance always positive?

00:36.379 --> 00:39.342
Well, even negative 6y can be positive

00:39.342 --> 00:41.802
if y is negative,

00:41.802 --> 00:43.020
so it's completely reasonable to say,

00:43.020 --> 00:45.597
well, this distance could be negative 6y.

00:45.597 --> 00:49.621
So the entire height right
over here is going to be,

00:49.621 --> 00:53.986
it's going to be y squared minus 6y.

00:53.986 --> 00:57.540
Or you could do it as y
squared plus this distance,

00:57.540 --> 01:00.976
which is negative 6y, y
squared plus negative 6y,

01:00.976 --> 01:03.959
which is the same thing
as y squared minus 6y.

01:03.959 --> 01:06.705
So that's the height
of this big rectangle.

01:06.705 --> 01:08.726
What's its width?

01:08.726 --> 01:11.813
Well, the width is going to be the width

01:11.813 --> 01:16.410
of this purple rectangle,
it's going to be 3y squared,

01:16.410 --> 01:19.498
plus the width of this yellow rectangle,

01:19.498 --> 01:22.795
which is negative 2y, and that
can have a negative out here,

01:22.795 --> 01:24.769
the same logic why this
could have a negative,

01:24.769 --> 01:26.812
why the negative 6y could have a negative,

01:26.812 --> 01:29.437
and then plus the width

01:29.437 --> 01:31.847
of the blue rectangle.

01:31.847 --> 01:33.454
And so if you add them all together,

01:33.454 --> 01:36.476
the width of the entire rectangle is going

01:36.476 --> 01:41.394
to be 3y squared minus 2y,

01:41.394 --> 01:43.848
minus 2y plus one.

01:44.738 --> 01:47.594
And just like that, this
expression that I just wrote down

01:47.594 --> 01:51.401
will give us the area for the entire,

01:51.401 --> 01:54.884
the area for the entire big rectangle.

01:54.884 --> 01:56.138
Now, there's another way to do it,

01:56.138 --> 01:59.366
and a big clue was that we
subdivided the big rectangle

01:59.366 --> 02:01.595
into these six smaller rectangles,

02:01.595 --> 02:04.311
and we have the dimensions for
the six smaller rectangles.

02:04.311 --> 02:06.006
And so we could find the
area for each of these,

02:06.006 --> 02:08.167
and then we could add them all together.

02:08.167 --> 02:09.629
So let's look at this first one.

02:09.629 --> 02:10.837
Height times width.

02:10.837 --> 02:13.297
The area of this purple
rectangle is gonna be the height,

02:13.297 --> 02:16.245
y squared, times the width,

02:16.245 --> 02:18.605
which is 3y squared,

02:18.605 --> 02:21.447
which is going to be equal
to, it's gonna be three,

02:21.447 --> 02:25.859
and then y squared times y
squared is y to the fourth power.

02:25.859 --> 02:27.275
What's the area of this yellow rectangle?

02:27.275 --> 02:28.877
Height is y squared.

02:28.877 --> 02:31.223
It's going to be y
squared times the width,

02:31.223 --> 02:33.359
times negative 2y,

02:33.359 --> 02:37.886
which is going to give us
negative 2y to the third power.

02:37.886 --> 02:39.117
What about the blue one?

02:39.117 --> 02:42.949
Well, height times width, it's
gonna be y squared times one,

02:42.949 --> 02:46.338
which, of course, is just
going to be equal to y squared.

02:46.338 --> 02:48.474
Now, this green one,
it's gonna be the height,

02:48.474 --> 02:52.746
which is now negative 6y, times the width,

02:52.746 --> 02:57.274
which is 3y squared, which
is going to be equal to,

02:57.274 --> 03:01.012
let's see, negative six
times three is negative 18,

03:01.012 --> 03:05.656
and then y times y squared
is y to the third power.

03:05.656 --> 03:08.977
Now, the area of this gray
rectangle is gonna be the height,

03:08.977 --> 03:12.869
which is negative 6y, times the width,

03:12.869 --> 03:15.818
which is negative 2y,

03:15.818 --> 03:18.488
which gets us negative
six times negative two

03:18.488 --> 03:20.225
is positive 12,

03:20.225 --> 03:23.755
y times y is y squared.

03:23.755 --> 03:26.591
And then finally the area of
this rectangle right over here,

03:26.591 --> 03:30.259
it's gonna be the height,
which is negative 6y,

03:30.259 --> 03:32.907
times the width, which is just one,

03:32.907 --> 03:35.995
which is equal to negative 6y.

03:35.995 --> 03:38.410
And so if we want the area
of this entire rectangle,

03:38.410 --> 03:41.034
we can just add up the
areas of the smaller ones,

03:41.034 --> 03:44.401
so it's going to be equal to the three,

03:44.401 --> 03:47.976
it's going to be equal
to the 3y to the fourth,

03:47.976 --> 03:51.272
3y to the fourth,

03:51.272 --> 03:55.406
plus negative 2y to the third power.

03:55.406 --> 03:59.307
Let me write this in a color
that corresponds to that.

03:59.307 --> 04:03.278
Negative 2y to the third power,

04:03.278 --> 04:05.234
plus y squared,

04:06.644 --> 04:10.801
plus y squared,

04:10.801 --> 04:14.259
minus 18y to the third power,

04:14.259 --> 04:18.765
so minus 18y to the third power,

04:18.765 --> 04:21.783
plus 12y squared.

04:21.783 --> 04:23.362
Let's write that in black.

04:23.362 --> 04:26.404
So plus 12y squared,

04:26.404 --> 04:30.607
and then last but not
least, we have the minus 6y,

04:30.607 --> 04:32.302
minus 6y.

04:32.302 --> 04:35.134
So this is an expression for
the area of the entire thing,

04:35.134 --> 04:36.946
but we can simplify it more.

04:36.946 --> 04:40.800
So let's see, we only have
one fourth degree term,

04:40.800 --> 04:42.843
so I'll just rewrite that.

04:42.843 --> 04:47.719
So we have one fourth degree term,

04:47.719 --> 04:48.740
so I'll just rewrite that.

04:48.740 --> 04:50.877
3y to the fourth power.

04:50.877 --> 04:53.500
Now, how many third
degree terms do we have?

04:53.500 --> 04:57.309
We have negative 2y to the third power.

04:57.309 --> 05:00.676
We have negative 18y to the third power.

05:00.676 --> 05:01.953
So if we add these two together,

05:01.953 --> 05:03.671
how many y to the third powers do we have?

05:03.671 --> 05:06.782
Well, negative two plus
negative 18 is negative 20,

05:06.782 --> 05:10.438
negative 20y to the third power.

05:10.438 --> 05:13.913
And then how many second
degree terms do we have?

05:13.913 --> 05:16.117
Well, we have one y
squared right over here,

05:16.117 --> 05:18.253
and then we have another, 12y squareds.

05:18.253 --> 05:22.804
You add those together, you're
gonna have 13y squareds.

05:22.804 --> 05:27.703
And then finally we still
need to subtract the 6y.

05:27.703 --> 05:28.841
And there you have it,

05:28.841 --> 05:32.835
another expression for the
area of the entire rectangle.

05:32.835 --> 05:34.716
And the whole point of
doing this is to realize

05:34.716 --> 05:38.083
that this up here and this
down here are equivalent,

05:38.083 --> 05:41.147
and that the way that we multiply
this actually corresponds

05:41.147 --> 05:42.912
to exactly how we found the areas

05:42.912 --> 05:45.234
of the smaller rectangles right over here.

05:45.234 --> 05:48.601
You would say y squared times
3y squared is 3y fourth.

05:48.601 --> 05:51.085
Y squared times negative 2y is negative 2y

05:51.085 --> 05:52.153
to the third power.

05:52.153 --> 05:56.681
Y squared times one is y squared,

05:56.681 --> 05:58.840
which is exactly what we
did when we found the area

05:58.840 --> 06:00.984
of these rectangles in
this, I guess you could say,

06:00.984 --> 06:02.114
in this top row.

06:02.114 --> 06:03.716
And then you would take the negative six,

06:03.716 --> 06:07.153
and you would say negative
six times 3y squared

06:07.153 --> 06:09.149
is negative 18y to the third.

06:09.149 --> 06:13.190
Negative six times negative
2y is positive 12y squared.

06:13.190 --> 06:17.313
Negative 6y times one

06:17.313 --> 06:19.903
is negative 6y.

06:19.903 --> 06:21.726
And just to realize that
this isn't just some type

06:21.726 --> 06:22.707
of voodoo that we're doing.

06:22.707 --> 06:24.821
It completely makes sense
when you think about

06:24.821 --> 06:27.753
in terms of an area model like this.
